SPRINT 2 — RATIO ENGINE EDGE CASE LOG
======================================

D08 — PROFITABILITY
- Sales = 0: NPM and OPM return None.
- Equity + reserves <= 0: ROE returns None.
- Capital employed = 0: ROCE returns None.
- OPM source values may differ because source percentages are rounded.

D09 — LEVERAGE & EFFICIENCY
- Debt-to-equity returns None when equity + reserves <= 0.
- Debt-free companies return 0 for debt-to-equity.
- Interest = 0 returns 999 for interest coverage, representing debt-free handling.
- Total assets = 0 returns None for asset turnover.

D10 — CAGR
- CAGR requires a positive starting and ending value.
- Non-positive values return None.
- Turnaround is flagged when the starting value is negative and ending value is positive.

D11 — CASH FLOW
- FCF is calculated as CFO + CFI and may be negative.
- CapEx intensity returns None when sales = 0.
- FCF conversion returns None when net profit = 0.
- CFO quality score returns None when net profit = 0.
- Capital allocation classification is based on CFO, CFI and CFF signs.

D12 — DATABASE
- 1,073 financial ratio rows were populated from the available source company-year records.
- 92 companies are represented.
- Source data contains 41 distinct year values.

D13 — BANKS/NBFCs
- Calculated year-level ROCE differs from the company-level source ROCE.
- Differences are documented in output/sector_roce_notes.csv.
- Differences are treated as methodology/data-basis differences rather than automatically classified as calculation errors.